# Superwork Workflow

## Overview

This project uses `.superwork/` as the local workflow and spec runtime.

## Package Map

{{ package_map }}

## Required Entry Points

1. Use `superwork-init` when `.superwork/` is missing or incomplete.
2. Use `superwork-start` at the beginning of every coding task.
3. Route bug work to `superwork-debugging`.
4. For non-bug work, classify the task as light, medium, or heavy by the shortest path that still meets quality requirements.
5. Route light tasks to `superwork-tdd`; use an inline TDD plan and do not require `.superwork/plans/*.md`.
6. Route medium tasks to `superwork-writing-plans`, save `.superwork/plans/*.md`, then continue with `superwork-executing-plans`.
7. Route heavy tasks by default to `superwork-brainstorming`, then `superwork-writing-plans`, then `superwork-executing-plans`.
8. Users may still invoke `superwork-brainstorming` manually on other non-bug tasks when extra design work is useful.
9. After `superwork-start` decides the route, it must explicitly state the chosen route and one short reason before handoff.
10. Execute all work directly on the current branch unless the user explicitly says otherwise.
11. Route finished implementation and bugfix work to `superwork-check`.
12. Require `superwork-check` to own the explicit `superwork-code-simplifier` decision: if the diff is medium or large, it must run `superwork-code-simplifier`; otherwise it may skip only with an explicit reason and must state why.
13. Require `superwork-check` to make an explicit `superwork-update-spec` decision (`update/create/no-update`), and default to `no-update` when no durable rule or contract changed.

## Workflow Contract

Treat the tagged blocks below as the machine-readable source of truth for routing, phase state, and next-step hints. Human-readable sections in this file must stay aligned with these blocks.

[superwork-route:bug]
kind: bug
skill: superwork-debugging
summary: Fix bugs, failing tests, regressions, or unexpected behavior through root-cause investigation first.
next: reproduce-the-problem-and-confirm-root-cause
[/superwork-route:bug]

[superwork-route:light]
kind: non-bug-light
skill: superwork-tdd
summary: Use the light path for single-file or small-scope work with an inline TDD plan.
next: write-inline-tdd-plan-then-run-red-green
[/superwork-route:light]

[superwork-route:medium]
kind: non-bug-medium
skill: superwork-writing-plans
summary: Use the medium path for clear multi-file work that needs a saved implementation plan.
next: write-plan-with-global-constraints-and-interfaces
[/superwork-route:medium]

[superwork-route:heavy]
kind: non-bug-heavy
skill: superwork-brainstorming
summary: Use the heavy path when design reduction is still needed before planning.
next: design-first-then-write-plan-then-execute
[/superwork-route:heavy]

[superwork-state:no_task]
phase: start
next: read-workflow-and-classify-the-task
hint: No active work yet. Use `superwork-start`, read this workflow, classify the task, and route to the lightest path that still preserves quality.
[/superwork-state:no_task]

[superwork-state:light_execution]
phase: tdd
next: write-inline-tdd-plan-then-run-red-green
hint: Stay on the light path. Do not create a saved plan file. Prove the change with RED before production edits.
[/superwork-state:light_execution]

[superwork-state:plan_execution]
phase: execute
next: run-plan-preflight-then-start-task-1
hint: Execute from the saved `.superwork/plans/*.md` plan. Run the one-time execution preflight before any code changes, then follow tasks in order.
[/superwork-state:plan_execution]

[superwork-state:debug_execution]
phase: debug
next: reproduce-investigate-add-regression-test-then-fix
hint: Stay in debugging until the root cause is confirmed and captured by a failing regression test.
[/superwork-state:debug_execution]

[superwork-state:completion]
phase: verify
next: route-through-superwork-check
hint: Finished implementation is not completion. Route through `superwork-check` for fresh verification, simplifier decision, and explicit spec update decision.
[/superwork-state:completion]

## Tooling Paths

- Context load: `superwork-start` (skill-internal tooling)
- Design docs: `.superwork/prd/*.md` (heavy-task design handoff from `superwork-brainstorming`)
- Durable rules and contracts: `.superwork/spec/**/*.md`
- Plan artifacts: `.superwork/plans/*.md` (implementation plans consumed by `superwork-executing-plans`)
- Spec check: `superwork-check` (skill-internal tooling)
- Spec update decision: `superwork-update-spec` (skill-internal tooling)
- Never generate or copy `scripts/*.py` into this project as runtime output.

## Default Verification Hints

- Prefer `{{ package_manager }}` commands when Node tooling is present.
- Choose light / medium / heavy by the shortest path that still meets quality requirements.
- After `superwork-start` classifies the task, state the chosen route and one short reason before invoking the next skill.
- Use `superwork-tdd` for light work: single-file or small-scope changes, config or copy tweaks, small test additions, or local doc updates. Keep the plan inline and do not force a saved plan file.
- Use `superwork-writing-plans` -> `superwork-executing-plans` for medium work that has clear scope but real multi-file coordination.
- Use `superwork-brainstorming` -> `superwork-writing-plans` -> `superwork-executing-plans` as the default heavy-work path when work is large, cross-cutting, or still needs design reduction.
- `superwork-brainstorming` can also be invoked manually on other non-bug tasks when the user wants extra design exploration before planning.
- Use `superwork-code-simplifier` only after behavior is verified, never as a substitute for TDD or debugging, and let `superwork-check` decide whether it must run.
- follow the completion policy through `superwork-check`; that stage owns the simplifier decision, fresh verification, and the explicit `superwork-update-spec` decision.
- Re-read the relevant spec indexes before implementation and before completion.
- Update specs only when new durable rules, contracts, edge cases, or test requirements appear.
